# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Nima Karimitari et al. (2026). Systematic fine-tuning of MACE interatomic potentials for catalysis.
#   npj Computational Materials. doi:10.1038/s41524-026-02335-z
#
# Version read: publisher (sha256 1013e876b027de21...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 593 (Training/reliability). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/karimitari2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the three from-scratch MACE models (FS-BMA, FS-BMA+MD,
# FS-All) and the six MACE models fine-tuned from MACE-MH-1 (OMAT head)
# with multi-head replay on catalysis training sets assembled from
# relaxation trajectories, MD and contour-exploration sampling. All
# accuracy figures in the paper are reaction-energy and activation-energy
# MAEs on downstream test sets, which are property errors and have no
# result.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
