###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# The paper reports no training-cost or inference-cost figures.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Every accuracy number (Tables 3 and 4, text) is a reaction-energy (Er) or activation-energy (Ea) MAE in eV on downstream catalysis test sets, or a fraction of adsorption energies within 0.2 eV; these are property errors and are not encoded. No energy or force test errors are stated.
# - FS-BMA+MD (47,651 configurations) and FT-BMA+MD(M) (44,959) are not encoded as runs: their training sets are combinations not separately described. The FS learning rate is given only relative to the FT one ('two orders of magnitude' larger) and is not encoded.
# - MACE-MH-1, UMA (OC20, OMAT heads) and MACE-MP0 are compared only on Er/Ea; MACE-MH-1 has no registry row, so it is a paper-local 'as distributed' run.
# - The BMA set (row 1 of Table 1) is a 20,000-structure selection from a published dataset (ref. 32); Table 1 gives 39,983 configurations (first and last frames).
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/karimitari2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.
